{"_id":"c401000000000001","description":"A d20 table of notable stalls and rumours for any market that owes the Saltmarket a debt of style.","displayRoll":true,"flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"8207464f0006c08dd2c30273189b67a84ef8fc79d50e1141cd2dd4907b2bda1e","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"saltmarket-curiosities","kind":"table","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"One notable stall, rumour or货源 at the Saltmarket Exchange."}},"folder":null,"formula":"1d12","name":"Saltmarket Curiosities","ownership":{"default":0},"replacement":true,"results":[{"_id":"tr01010000000000","description":"A broker sells sealed jars of 'last spring's honest rain'. One of them is sealed with the buyer's own seal.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[1,1],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01020000000000","description":"A map vendor sells honest maps of dishonest places, priced by the number of ways off them.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[2,2],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01030000000000","description":"A stall of charter papers: passage rights to three bridges, one gate, and a well that has never been dry.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[3,3],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01040000000000","description":"A dwarf buys broken locks by weight and pays in keys that will someday open them.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[4,4],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01050000000000","description":"An auction of unclaimed luggage from a ferry that never sank is cancelled; the luggage won.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[5,5],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01060000000000","description":"A shop of tide-good clocks, each correct twice a day and generous about which twice.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[6,6],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01070000000000","description":"Three merchants sell the same sword's biography, with rising and irreconcilable detail.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[7,7],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01080000000000","description":"A broker offers 'rented courage per hour', with a deposit and a very earnest return policy.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[8,8],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01090000000000","description":"A cellar specialises in the inventories of three dead merchants, cross-referenced and faintly haunted by paperwork.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[9,9],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01100000000000","description":"Someone is quietly buying every copy of one specific folk song.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[10,10],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01110000000000","description":"A lantern-oil stand sells one odourless grade and one that smells like whoever you miss.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[11,11],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr01120000000000","description":"The house scale of the Exchange broke; brokers now argue prices with their hands tied behind their backs.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[12,12],"type":"text","weight":1}],"sort":100}
{"_id":"c402000000000001","description":"A d20 table of evening quietly-noticed events for any camp, wayhouse or dock with a light left on.","displayRoll":true,"flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"f3d12268bb094197b30ac68079fa57d160628e085f52c232f3738f207fa41d79","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"porchlight-nights","kind":"table","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"The small events of a night under the Compact's lamp."}},"folder":null,"formula":"1d12","name":"Porchlight Nights","ownership":{"default":0},"replacement":true,"results":[{"_id":"tr02010000000000","description":"The watchfire is already lit when the group arrives; nobody will admit to lighting it.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[1,1],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02020000000000","description":"A keeper leaves soup out with a note: 'The pot is for the cold, not the curious.'","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[2,2],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02030000000000","description":"An owl repairs the silence twice during the night watch, once on purpose.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[3,3],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02040000000000","description":"A lantern token arrives by bird, flipped; someone owes someone, urgently.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[4,4],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02050000000000","description":"The kettle disagrees with the night and stays warm anyway.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[5,5],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02060000000000","description":"Someone's horse learns one word of the local language; it is the worst possible word.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[6,6],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02070000000000","description":"The night wind reads aloud from a gamblers' left-behind letter, softly, twice.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[7,7],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02080000000000","description":"All the stars agree that the north is somewhere important tonight.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[8,8],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02090000000000","description":"A stranger's coat dries by the fire with more pockets in the morning than at night.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[9,9],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02100000000000","description":"The road behind reports three travellers who passed singing; nobody hears the tune in daylight.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[10,10],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02110000000000","description":"A willow spends the night leaning an inch closer to the tent, thinking better of it by dawn.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[11,11],"type":"text","weight":1},{"_id":"tr02120000000000","description":"Dawn arrives on schedule and the dogs negotiate for nine more minutes.","documentUuid":null,"drawn":false,"flags":{},"img":"","name":"","range":[12,12],"type":"text","weight":1}],"sort":200}
